Keep related heading, support copy and CTA together. Position an existing requested image as part of the chosen composition rather than always appending it after all text. Choose background presentation only when requested or appropriate under server constraints and legible with supplied registered roles. Do not invent a visual request to fill an empty column or move sources across units. Respect the mandatory imageRequirements independently of aesthetic choices.
Preserve the shell and all non-children fields exactly. Do not change ancestor geometry, reserved shells or sibling regions to achieve an unsupported composition. Do not add fixed text heights, new CSS, arbitrary gaps or unsupported positioning. Maintain readable normal flow, heading order and the approved source-assignment transport.
Provide explicit responsive overrides only where a supplied default would give an unsuitable order or ratio; otherwise keep safe null defaults. Desktop composition may differ from mobile''s safe single-column flow. Use the runtime''s existing layout, source, media and style fields only; do not emit this design process as page copy or new JSON fields.'),
('promo_page_schema_planner', '# COMPOSITION SELECTION WITHIN THE EXISTING CONTRACT
For a fresh page, evaluate two or three compact composition possibilities before selecting one content-led tree in this same call. Return one PageSchema only; do not expose alternatives, planning prose, scoring objects or additional calls. Choose emphasis, content/image relationship, density and rhythm before allocating generic elements. Do not automatically reuse a hero plus equal cards plus CTA sequence.
Read explicit preferences in designBrief.requestText, revisionRequest and explicitRequirements as bounded task data even when a parsed hero field is null. Mood alone does not dictate geometry. Use supplied recent composition outlines only when present; do not invent a history or claim uniqueness.
For an edit, follow the supplied instruction, selected scope and currentPage. An explicit request to rearrange a permitted area may change that area''s layout; a copy-only request preserves geometry. Generic diversity guidance is never permission to discard the page, exceed the selected scope, remove required sources or override server preservation rules. If the request is simply to resume/view the current result, preserve it.
Choose explicit layout on meaningful layout-bearing groups. Use supported grid ratios/spans and row/column relationships deliberately. Avoid grouping every section as the same full-width column merely because it is valid. Equal repeated cards are useful for comparable benefits; editorial sections, a key offer, instructions and supporting legal copy can have different hierarchy and density when the content justifies it. These are composition criteria, not a fixed list of required sections.
Use only the supplied geometry and registered grid/spacing choices. Keep text widths readable and normal-flow heights driven by content. Do not invent offsets, min-height, arbitrary sizes, CSS or breakpoints. Honor server constraints on image presentation; where a background key visual is required, vary supported copy grouping, alignment, neighboring content and CTA emphasis within that requirement rather than violating it. Do not assume a body prompt can override a server constraint.
Keep every required factual source intact, retain permitted prepared assets and bind requested images correctly. Select a coherent tree within existing node/depth/response budgets, without multiplying elements or images for visual novelty. Use existing summary/warnings fields only where the schema permits and a limitation actually needs reporting. Do not add workflow or design-decision metadata.'),
('section_background_image', '# GGPOKER-INSPIRED VISUAL CRAFT
Use the GGPoker-inspired promotional craft profile as a written art-direction reference for this application. It guides material quality, lighting, focal clarity and production finish, not a compulsory brand identity, poker subject, palette or layout. Explicit campaign direction, the approved image intent and supplied palette take precedence. A non-poker request keeps its own subject matter. Do not add poker props, a casino scene, red/gold colouring or a logo merely because this profile is available.
For requested poker material, render recognisable card/chip/table/bonus objects only when supported by the approved intent. Use convincing proportions, restrained polished materials, controlled specular highlights, grounded shadows, dimensional separation and an uncluttered focal point. Choose a photographic or premium 3D treatment appropriate to the request; do not combine unrelated stock scenes, excessive glow or decorative clutter to suggest quality. Never invent players, endorsements, promotional claims or branded marks.
Treat contentJson.visualReference.mode written-art-direction and referenceImageCount 0 as evidence that no reference photograph has been supplied. Do not claim to have viewed GGPoker''s website, copied a specific campaign image, inspected a screenshot or matched a reference photograph. A URL mentioned in copy is not an image input. Use only the supplied image intent, designBrief and validated target; do not fetch reference URLs or introduce a new reference requirement.
Use contentJson.brandPalette when present, or the supplied background/palette variables, to keep the visual coherent with the page. Natural lighting and photographic shading need not quantise every image pixel to CSS tokens; they must not become arbitrary page CSS values. Do not change page tokens, geometry, source copy, image IDs or action bindings.
Keep headings, promotional amounts, CTA labels and legal copy out of the generated pixels. Do not invent a logo, watermark, trophy inscription, certification or text badge. The renderer supplies campaign text and registered identity assets separately. A visual must not imply an unsupported benefit or award.

# HERO / BACKGROUND COMPOSITION
Compose one coherent key visual for contentJson.target and the requested aspect ratio. Respect the shared brief''s explicit copy-safe area. When that area is not specified, use supplied text/group relationships as qualitative guidance, without claiming pixel coordinates. Keep high-frequency detail and the focal subject away from the intended copy area while retaining a complete scene across the remaining canvas. Preserve crop-safe subjects across the actual requested ratio; do not invent a second mobile image or change the page layout.
Use tonal separation, depth and controlled light to support real foreground text. Respect fadeMode, including none; do not bake an unrequested gradient, opaque text panel or fake button into the image. Do not force a centered hero or always place the subject on the same side: compose for the actual target. If a contrast treatment requires a page overlay, only the renderer''s registered overlay may provide it.'),
('component_image', '# GGPOKER-INSPIRED VISUAL CRAFT
Use the GGPoker-inspired promotional craft profile as a written art-direction reference for this application. It guides material quality, lighting, focal clarity and production finish, not a compulsory brand identity, poker subject, palette or layout. Explicit campaign direction, the approved image intent and supplied palette take precedence. A non-poker request keeps its own subject matter. Do not add poker props, a casino scene, red/gold colouring or a logo merely because this profile is available.
