Treat contentJson.visualReference.mode written-art-direction and referenceImageCount 0 as evidence that no reference photograph has been supplied. Do not claim to have viewed GGPoker''s website, copied a specific campaign image, inspected a screenshot or matched a reference photograph. A URL mentioned in copy is not an image input. Use only the supplied image intent, designBrief and validated target; do not fetch reference URLs or introduce a new reference requirement.
Use contentJson.brandPalette when present, or the supplied background/palette variables, to keep the visual coherent with the page. Natural lighting and photographic shading need not quantise every image pixel to CSS tokens; they must not become arbitrary page CSS values. Do not change page tokens, geometry, source copy, image IDs or action bindings.
Keep headings, promotional amounts, CTA labels and legal copy out of the generated pixels. Do not invent a logo, watermark, trophy inscription, certification or text badge. The renderer supplies campaign text and registered identity assets separately. A visual must not imply an unsupported benefit or award.

# COMPONENT / CARD COMPOSITION
Compose for this component''s specific approved intent, role and crop. A benefit object, participation illustration and supporting atmosphere may need different subject scale and viewpoint while sharing the page''s material/lighting direction. Do not repeat the hero scene or identical chip pile on every card, and do not invent extra objects or claims solely to make images different. Preserve continuity where related items should look comparable.
Keep the principal subject recognisable at card size, with clean edges, purposeful depth and safe crop margins. Do not turn every component image into a full promotional banner with embedded headings or CTA. When component_image is used for a background target, follow contentJson.target.purpose and its copy-safe relationship rather than assuming a standalone square card. Return only the configured image output and keep the supplied aspect ratio.')
)
select p.type,p.id,p.status,p.version,
  case when p.status='active' then 'already active with guidance'
       when p.status='validated' then 'already validated with guidance'
       else 'body prepared; validate and activate in Admin' end as next_step
from prompt_templates p
join expected e on e.prompt_type=p.type
where p.status in ('draft','validated','active') and p.archived_at is null
  and position(e.recognition_body in p.body)>0
  and exists (
    select 1 from prompt_templates active_prompt
    where active_prompt.type=p.type and active_prompt.lineage_id=p.lineage_id
      and active_prompt.status='active' and active_prompt.archived_at is null
  )
order by p.type,p.version;
